I think your pet should never attack the oracle, your Quest leader,
your leader's minions, and any co-aligned priest. It's just annoying.
On the other hand, how would your pet know that you don't want it to
kill them? So, although it is annoying, it sems logical to me. Your pet
attacks anything it takes it can handle, so it should not distinguish
between foes. After all, how would he see the difference between a
shopkeeper you want him to kill and one you don't?

Another possibility mentioned above would be to have your pet attack NO
peaceful creatures. This would be consistent, but I wouldn't like it.
Having your pet attack them is the only way to get rid of peaceful
creatures without lowering your alignment, and I wouldn't want to lose
this possiblity (I hate those peaceful dwarfs that ruin my dungeon
lay-out!).

